## 3. Design in one paragraph

The v2 residual stream is *defined* as the image of the source trunk's residual stream under one fixed orthonormal width chart `C` (5120 -> 2048, rank-2048 PCA of the pooled post-attention residual rows). Every v2 tensor is then a fold: reads from the stream become `C^T diag(w_norm) W_src^T` (norm weights folded in), writes to the stream become `W_src C`, heads are selected whole (exact per head) from a pool of 2-3 same-kind source layers and their output projections are ridge-refitted against the pooled source writes, FFNs are a union coreset (C2/C10/C14 machinery) over the pooled trunk channels, the K3 form-E channels lifted through the refolded C17 charts, and the media-unit channels, with the down projection ridge-refitted on the **folded prefix's own rows** (dual stream, the K3 ruling's item 2). The raw boundary rows and the x0 head are closed-form ridge fits from raw units to teacher activations and from folded-trunk features to clean raw units. Nothing is copied; nothing is trained; every finite fit number is a diagnostic; the only gates are structural/non-finite checks, the >= 4x per-component rule, and decoded behaviour.

Data flow:

