## 4. Design: which source supplies which v2 tensor

### 4.1 The width fold (5120 -> 2048; 7168 -> 2048 for K3)

**Decision: one global orthonormal stream chart `C` per source stream, not per-layer charts, for the stream itself.** A residual stream only makes sense in one basis: a write made at layer k in basis `C_k` is read at layer k+1 through `C_{k+1}`; if they differ the error `C_k C_{k+1}^+ - I` lands in every token. Per-layer charts are exactly what C17 fits, but C17 charts between two *independently existing* streams (K3 and the trunk), and that is still how K3 and the units enter (4.3-4.4).

- `C` [5120 x 2048], orthonormal columns: the top-2048 principal directions of the **centred** post-attention residual rows pooled over all 64 T layers on the text calibration corpus (subsample about 500k rows; the gram is 5120^2 in fp64 on the CPU: seconds). v2 has no biases, so the row mean is kept as the first chart direction instead of a bias (its energy recorded), the way C17's SVD arm folds the mean into its biases.
- **Norm fold.** Every pre-norm read `y = (h / rms(h)) * w . W^T` becomes, with `h_src ~ h_v2 C^T`: `y ~ (h_v2 / rms_v2) . s_k . C^T diag(w) W^T`. So the v2 projection is `C^T diag(w) W_src^T` (exact linear algebra) and the v2 RMSNorm weight is the scalar `s_k = mean(rms_src / rms_v2)` on the calibration rows (one scalar per norm; the elementwise `w` has been absorbed). Record `s_k` and its spread; the spread is the only approximation.
- **Diagnostics recorded, never gates:** retained energy per layer under `C`, per-layer relL2 of `h_src` vs `h_v2 C^T`, the spread of `s_k`.
- **Ablation arm F-C2 (experiments lane):** per-AttnRes-block charts `C_b` (6 charts) with the block boundary absorbing the basis change through the zero-init AttnRes (the partial sum resets at every depth boundary [V spec section 1]). Not the default: it is novel; the global chart is the boring option.
- K3 and the units reach the v2 stream through chart **composition**: `C_{K3->v2} = C_{K3->T} . C`, where `C_{K3->T}` is the refolded C17 ridge chart (7168 -> 5120, per trunk layer, fitted on paired tokens). Composition is exact linear algebra and lets the CPU C17 refold run in parallel with everything else. **Arm F-K3DIRECT** refits C17 directly against the folded v2 prefix rows (K3 7168 <-> v2 2048) inside the sequential loop; closer to the ruling's "fitted on its own prefix", but it serialises about 12 h of CPU fitting into the GPU loop. Build the composed version first, the direct one as the second arm.

### 4.2 The depth fold

**Trunk (T or S5) -> v2: period-aligned, kind-preserving.** Both have the `(kda,kda,kda,gated_gqa)` period, so align *periods*, then slot j of the v2 period receives slot j of every pooled source period. Floor-interval map (C17's convention):

| v2 period p (`co2-2b`, 6 periods) | source periods `[floor(16p/6), floor(16(p+1)/6))` | v2 layers | source layers pooled per slot |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | {0, 1} | 0-3 | 2 |
| 1 | {2, 3, 4} | 4-7 | 3 |
| 2 | {5, 6, 7} | 8-11 | 3 |
| 3 | {8, 9, 10} | 12-15 | 3 |
| 4 | {11, 12} | 16-19 | 2 |
| 5 | {13, 14, 15} | 20-23 | 3 |

`co2-4b` (8 periods): exactly 2 source periods per v2 period. The map lives in `alignment.json` (schema as C17's `{schema, summary, table}`), written before any fit (step P2).

**K3 (92 MoE layers + dense L0) -> v2 layers: floor-interval 92:24.** v2 layer k receives K3 MoE layers `[1 + floor(92k/24), 1 + floor(92(k+1)/24))`: 20 layers get 4 K3 layers, 4 get 3; K3 dense L0 joins v2 layer 0's pool (as C17's `--dense-layer0 trunk0`). For the 4B, 92:32 (28 layers get 3, 4 get 2). K3's own mixer kinds (3 KDA : 1 MLA, AttnRes block 12) do not line up with v2's slots; that is irrelevant for FFN pooling (an FFN is an FFN) and is one reason K3 mixers are an arm, not the default (4.3).

**Units -> v2 layers:** each unit is one parent block at a known relative depth (`charted_block.json` `insert_after` and the parent's depth [R]); it lands on the v2 layer at the same relative depth, recorded in `alignment.json`. Arm F-UMID: all five on the AttnRes block that holds layer 12 (OMNI1 put them mid-trunk at blocks 32-36 of 69 [V OMNI1 config]).

**Multi-layer merge is the one genuinely lossy step.** Pooling 2-3 source layers into one means one v2 layer must write what 2-3 source layers wrote, from the input the *first* of them saw. The ridge refit of every output projection takes `x_k` (v2 prefix rows) as input and `sum over l in pool of write_l(h_l) . C` as target; the held relL2 of that fit is the merge's honest diagnostic (expect worse than C17's single-layer numbers; it is recorded, never a gate).

