### 4.6 The objective, per Cyril's folding rules

- **Closed form only.** Every fit is a ridge or an SVD; no optimizer, no backward pass (the 2026-08-13 A1 ruling: "finding optimized folded versions, not training").
- **Dual stream / own prefix.** Layer k is fitted on the rows the already-folded v2 prefix produces (`x_k`), against the source's writes at the paired positions (item 2 of the K3 ruling), so each fold's error is absorbed by the next fit.
- **Multi-token where possible.** (a) Targets are teacher-forced source writes over full 4,096-token sequences and full media spans, so every row's target carries its whole context. (b) **Block-end target arm F-BE:** for the last layer of each AttnRes depth block, the `down` / `out` targets are the source residual at the *block end* charted, minus the v2 prefix residual (what the block still has to write), i.e. a 4-layer look-ahead; closed form, first-order. Default off; built as an arm because it is the only place where "multi-token" changes the fit itself. (c) The whole-prefix divergence on held tokens (`stream_divergence.held.relL2`, as `k3_dense_pass` records) is computed at every block end and **recorded**.
- **Finite numbers are diagnostics.** relL2, cos, retained energy, update scale, chart-bias energy, merge loss: all recorded in the receipt and in omni_lab `metric` rows; none stops a layer (`--acceptance record` semantics everywhere). Structural, load, identity, provenance and non-finite checks remain functional refusals.
- **>= 4x per component** is a structural rule verified from tensor shapes in the receipt (4.4).
- **Token match is never a gate.** The held top-1 vs T is recorded as a diagnostic column only.

