## 6. Calibration data (mixed modalities, one sequence layout)

Every fit row is a position in a sequence laid out by `CO/src/chimera_omni/v2_layout.py` (`<|media|> header <|/hdr|> <|raw|> rows ...`), so media rows sit in the stream exactly as they will at runtime. Built once as `L/scratch/v2-fold/calib/v2fold_calib_v1.{safetensors,manifest.json}` with a sha recorded in omni_lab `dataset_version` before any fit.

| Band | Source | Rows (fit / held) [E] | Pairing |
|---|---|---|---|
| Text | `omni-evidence-27b-v1` (24 x 4,096 Qwen tokens; fit 69,743 / held 23,186 [R]) | 93k | K3 pairing via `boundary_map.json` (the only K3 pairing; K3 contributes targets on these rows only) |
| Image | `v2proxy_all_v1` COCO 1,642 train / 200 test photos as 32 px units (a 256^2 image = 64 rows) | about 105k / 13k | QVL32 L13 features for the boundary fit; captions as the text prefix (COCO 2017 captions on disk [R spec section 14.4]) |
| Video | `video_in.jsonl` 512 clips [R] plus the panned COCO clips of the proxy (12.5 fps, 2-frame tubelets as in round 3) | about 40k / 5k | frame features as above |
| Speech | LibriSpeech dev-clean (fit) / test-clean (held) speakers f/m, 80 ms units at 38.4 kHz | 32k / 4k | speech-teacher encoder features |
| Music | MAESTRO (own split) plus ACE renders | 32k / 4k | ACE unit input rows |
| 3D | ModelNet10 16^3 SDF, 8 rows per shape, with the time-token row (D3) | 10k / 1.6k | HY3D unit input rows |

Held splits are drawn on **trunk tokens / whole media items** (C17's rule: no token on both sides). Media rows carry *no* K3 target and no T target (both text-only); their FFN target is `TERM_units` and their mixer target is the pooled T mixers evaluated on the charted media rows (what T would write for that row: a consistent definition, recorded as such).

