## 9. Trade-offs

| Choice | Rejected alternative | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **T (run-1 student) as the default trunk source; S5 as the control arm** | S5 only (purest fold-only lineage) | T = S5's fold plus the full-KD that Cyril's 09-01 order allowed on top of a fold, and it is the better-behaved trunk (S5: held top-1 vs trunk 0.734, rq 0.862 [V `s5_metrics_full.json`]). The v2 weights are *folded from* T, not copied; the lineage is fold -> distill -> fold. **Flagged for Cyril (section 11): if he reads "built from folding" as fold-only lineage, the S5 arm is the base and T is dropped.** |
| **One global orthonormal stream chart** | per-layer ridge charts (C17 style) for the stream | a residual stream needs one basis; per-layer charts put a basis-change error into every token. Per-block charts kept as arm F-C2 |
| **Composed K3 charts `C_{K3->T} o C`** | direct per-layer K3 <-> v2 charts in the loop | composition is exact linear algebra and lets the 12 h CPU refold run in parallel; the direct fit is arm F-K3DIRECT |
| **Exact head transplant from T/S5 for mixers; K3 mixers as arms** | K3 KDA/MLA heads as the default mixer source (K3 = primary) | T/S5 have the same head dims as v2, so heads move exactly; K3's per-channel decay and NoPE MLA need approximations. K3's *knowledge* enters through every layer's FFN union (the ruling's "all experts, all layers"), which is where it lived in S5 too |
| **`w_k3 = 0.03` as default, 0.1 as arm** | full additive K3 term | the C10 design sweep measured the full union collapsing the trunk (top-1 7/210) [R `S7_DECISIONS` D4 note]; 0.03 is the design of record |
| **Union coreset over mixed rows, no per-source quotas** | reserved channel quotas per source or per modality | a quota is a type table by another name (R3/R5); the energy ranking on mixed rows lets media channels win where they fire |
| **Tied embed from the head side** | joint LS (arm), untied (arm) | logit fidelity is what the frozen review reads; the input-side mismatch is measured, and untying costs 510M phone-side params |
| **Boundary/head as ridge fits to teacher activations and clean units** | random init of boundary and head (spec section 9's earlier text) | the ruling forbids a non-folded weight; a closed-form fit to parent activations is a fold of the parent's behaviour, and it gives F4/F5 something to measure |
| **AttnRes query = 0** | random or copied | zero is function-preserving [V spec section 1]; it stores nothing |
| **Closed-form everywhere** | a few hundred SGD steps to "heal" the merge | Cyril: no training before capability; the A1 ruling allows closed-form optimised folds only |
| **Reuse `c17_chart_fit.py`, `c10_union_install.py` lifts, `c14_union_coreset.CoresetFold`, `run_omni_frozen_review.py`, `v2_proxy_mixed.py` instruments; new tools only as thin drivers** | a new monolithic "v2 folder" | the existing tools carry receipts, tests and the owner-policy semantics (`--acceptance record`, bias diagnostics) already |
| **P40 GPU3/GPU5 plus CPU, layer-streamed** | borrowing GPU6/GPU0/GPU4 | nothing here needs bf16 or more than about 6 GB VRAM per layer; the only long pole is the CPU C17 refold, which no card speeds up in fp64 |
| **No OC01 X00/X31 fallback for the 4B** | spec section 9 / A0b "best OC01 4B fold child" | those children are folds of Qwen3.5-4B, i.e. the excluded model with a different name; the 4B uses the same sources and recipe as the 2B |

